    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1039">

                <pb facs="0964" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Sa1/12</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-29T22:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1914, 10 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 30, 8 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your telegrams December 22, 7 p.m., December 28, 6 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1039-f1"/> Foreign Office informs me that unless <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sacramento</hi> leaves within twenty-four hours, as
                    notified to do through the American Consulate this afternoon, both ship and crew
                    will be interned. Consulate acting under the instructions of Department,
                    November 30, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1039-f2"/> is holding ship’s
                    papers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
